- `action(n1, "start review process")`: Hallucinates an initial step not present in the source; the description states the process begins directly by "reviewing the received application", which is correctly captured by `action(n2, ...)`.
- `action(n12, "end")`: Hallucinates a pre-terminal action; the source indicates the process will "come to an end" immediately after "write back the case data", making an intermediate step redundant when `end(e1)` already marks termination.
- `actor(a_default, "Default", [...])`: Misassigns responsibility; the source explicitly identifies "the review clerk" as the performer of all steps, but the model declares a generic "Default" actor.
- `action(n5, "are there any new findings")` and `action(n8, "are there any new findings again")`: Incorrectly treats decision checkpoints as executable action nodes preceding XOR branches; the source frames these strictly as conditional evaluations ("they need to check if..."), not as distinct actionable tasks.